`@web/site` belongs to the Builder origin family with MothSource backing. See
@../../#package-origins-and-backing (Package origins and backing) for the
package model. It requires an explicit `@web/site` dependency and isn't in the
implicit scope of `.mtf` files.

### Static URLs

`site.root` is a compile-time `String` containing the structural site root.
`site.url` joins that root to a site-relative suffix. The suffix must
not start with `/`. The root follows the consuming project's configured
`origin` when the builder renders the page.

The helper composes strings without validating routes, encoding or normalising
paths. It doesn't inspect the current page or browser. Use
@../page (@web/page) for live browser state. In particular, `site.url` builds
links at compile time while `page.url()` reads the current browser address at
runtime.
